+ * MMU faults by GIC interrupt (JOB = INTID 452, MMU = INTID 453, SPI 420/421; the GPU line 451 is not used) instead of the busy poll. The ISR never clears a
+ * Mali interrupt: it reads the source's STATUS (RAWSTAT & MASK), writes that source's MASK to 0 (the level line drops, RAWSTAT keeps the bits for check_job),
+ * sets a pending bit and wakes sm_thread. sm_thread re-arms the masks while a job is in flight and sleeps with a 2 ms fallback deadline instead of poll_us; a
+ * wakeup lost between its check and the sleep costs at most that fallback (counted as `fallback`), never a hang. Masks are 0 whenever the GPU is idle, reset or dead.
+ * IRQ mode is refused (polling stays) when the attach readback shows the SPI not in Group 1 or not enabled, and it falls back to polling with a GAP line if
+ * 200 jobs complete without a single JOB interrupt.
